---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
const lang = 'en';
const t = (await import('../../translations/en.json')).default;
---

<Layout lang={lang} title={t.nav.comparison} description="Simpli vs Indonesian, English, Esperanto, Glosa, Globish.">
  <h1>{t.nav.comparison}</h1>
  <p>Simpli vs Indonesian, English, Esperanto, Glosa, Globish.</p>

  <h2>Simple: "I see you"</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Language</th><th>Sentence</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Simpli</td><td><em>mi si yu</em></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Indonesian</td><td>Saya lihat kamu</td></tr>
      <tr><td>English</td><td>I see you</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Esperanto</td><td>Mi vidas vin</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Glosa</td><td>Mi vide tu</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Globish</td><td>I see you</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Medium: "Tomorrow, I will see you at my brother's house"</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Language</th><th>Sentence</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Simpli</td><td><em>tumoro mi si yu at haus broder mi</em></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Indonesian</td><td>Besok, saya akan bertemu Anda di rumah saudara laki-laki saya</td></tr>
      <tr><td>English</td><td>Tomorrow, I will see you at my brother's house</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Esperanto</td><td>Morgaŭ, mi vidos vin ĉe la domo de mia frato</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Glosa</td><td>Crasti, mi vide tu a dom de mi fratri</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Globish</td><td>Tomorrow, I will see you at my brother's house</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>More complex: "Next week I will go to the market to buy food for my family"</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Language</th><th>Sentence</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Simpli</td><td><em>nekst wik mi go tu markat tu get fud for famali mi</em></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Indonesian</td><td>Minggu depan saya akan pergi ke pasar untuk membeli makanan untuk keluarga saya</td></tr>
      <tr><td>English</td><td>Next week I will go to the market to buy food for my family</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Esperanto</td><td>Semajnon poste mi iros al la merkato por aĉeti manĝaĵon por mia familio</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Glosa</td><td>Proxi semani mi go a marketa e merka fag pro mi familia</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Globish</td><td>Next week I will go to the market to buy food for my family</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p><strong>Takeaway:</strong> Simpli is simpler than Esperanto, more regular than English, more intuitive than Glosa.</p>
  <p>
    Simpli is not “simplified English.” It does not aim to replace English. You can still learn English and enjoy
    English literature and books while using Simpli as an auxiliary bridge language.
  </p>
</Layout>
